{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"730","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"K. Roads Orientation Problem"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Berland consists of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" cities and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" bidirectional roads connecting pairs of cities. There is no road connecting a city to itself, and between any pair of cities there is no more than one road. It is possible to reach any city from any other moving along roads."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Currently Mr. President is in the city "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" and his destination is the city "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":". He plans to move along roads from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s ≠ t"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"That's why Ministry of Fools and Roads has difficult days. The minister is afraid that Mr. President could get into a traffic jam or get lost. Who knows what else can happen!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To be sure that everything goes as planned, the minister decided to temporarily make all roads one-way. So each road will be oriented in one of two possible directions. The following conditions must be satisfied:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" There should be no cycles along roads after orientation. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The city "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" should be the only such city that all its roads are oriented out (i.e. there are no ingoing roads to the city "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the city "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the only such city). "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The city "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" should be the only such city that all its roads are oriented in (i.e. there are no outgoing roads from the city "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the city "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the only such city). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help the minister solve his problem. Write a program to find any such orientation of all roads or report that no solution exists."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test in this problem contains one or more test cases to solve. The first line of the input contains positive number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of cases to solve."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each case starts with a line containing four integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 4·105"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ m ≤ 106"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ s, t ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s ≠ t"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of cities, the number of roads and indices of departure and destination cities. The cities are numbered from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain roads, one road per line. Each road is given as two integer numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xj"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"yj"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ xj, yj ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xj ≠ yj"},{"kind":"text","text":"), which means that the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th road connects cities "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xj"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"yj"},{"kind":"text","text":". There is at most one road between any pair of cities. It is possible to reach any city from any other moving along roads."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The sum of values "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" over all cases in a test doesn't exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4·105"},{"kind":"text","text":". The sum of values "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" over all cases in a test doesn't exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"106"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each case print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if the answer exists. In the following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines print roads in the required directions. You can print roads in arbitrary order. If there are multiple answers, print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the only line \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"No"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if there is no answer for a case."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n4 4 1 2\n1 2\n2 3\n3 4\n4 1\n3 2 1 3\n3 1\n2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"Yes\n1 2\n3 2\n4 3\n1 4\nNo\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"K","problemCode":"730K","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/730/problem/K"}